=== ACCEPTANCE (web parity: features/driving/components/drivetrain-health/TemperatureTrendChart.tsx) ===
- Surface renders every state the web source has: loading (header + skeleton), empty, ready (line chart +
  markers + accessible table). The web render gate — the parent first filters null-temperature points
  (chartData.filter(d => d.outsideTemp !== null)) and then `data.length <= 1 → return null` — maps to the
  friendly Empty state when fewer than two plottable points exist. The page owns error/stale/offline once
  for the whole Drivetrain-Health experience (the web chart has no fetch-driven branch of its own), so the
  surface's branch set is loading/empty/ready exactly as the web component.
- Data: bound via the shared P1/S8 state-holder model (TemperatureTrendChartModel: the web `data` prop +
  the parent fetch flag); no direct HTTP from the view. SI Celsius outside-temperature points
  (d.outsideTempAvgC) + the pre-formatted drive-date label (formatDateShort). Unit conversion happens only
  in the projection (useUnits boundary).
- Charts: native TsLineChart (web recharts LineChart) with one outside-temperature line (#06b6d4 → regen
  role), built-in legend (web <Legend/>), and two dashed HorizontalLine annotations — Warm Zone at 35°C
  (#f59e0b → energy role) and Freezing at 0°C (#06b6d4 → regen role) — the web <ReferenceLine> markers.
  Plus the accessible data-table expander (web ChartContainer dataColumns Date / Outside).
- Unit handling: native converts BOTH the line and the markers to the display unit at the single projection
  boundary, so the plotted line, the threshold markers, the Y unit and the column header agree. (The web
  plots the data raw °C while only converting its markers — a latent imperial-mode inconsistency; the native
  render corrects it per the SI-canonical display-boundary mandate + the StatorTempChart sibling precedent.
  Metric output is identical to the web; imperial is unit-consistent. Documented, not silent.) Verified:
  metric line 10/20 °C unchanged, imperial 50/68 °F; markers metric 35/0, imperial 95/32.
- i18n: all eight source keys resolve from the P1/S10 catalog — drivetrain.tempHistory / .tempHistorySub /
  .tempHistory.aria [added to en+he+ar] / col.date / col.outside / outsideTemp / warmZone / freezing — plus
  shared chart.noData + common.loading. Web parity preserved: the line legend label is the bare
  t('drivetrain.outsideTemp') with NO unit suffix; the unit travels on the series Unit + the column header.
  No English literals in native code (English fallbacks mirror the web t(key, fallback) defaults).
- a11y: Narrator name on the surface (per state), the chart (aria), the data-table expander and every data
  row (date + labelled unit-suffixed reading, em dash for a gap); reduced-motion honored via TsFadeIn
  (web <FadeIn delay={0.25}>); system font scale inherited.
